e87n-display for Debian
======================

This architecture-independent Python package targets the EdgePi E87N and
requires the board's NV3007 framebuffer and backlight kernel support.
The kernel remains the default fan controller. `fan test LEVEL SECONDS` is a
root-only, bounded diagnostic: it briefly requests a thermal cooling level and
restores the previous level; it is not a persistent manual mode. The 428x142
screen shows kernel mode, cooling level and PWM percentage only; it deliberately
does not display tachometer RPM. No provisioning, account,
network, firmware or kernel installation is performed by this package.

Commands:
  e87nctl status
  e87nctl doctor
  e87nctl fan status
  e87nctl fan test 1 5
  e87nctl acceleration status
  e87nctl display config
  e87nctl display brightness 20
  e87nctl display screen thermal
  e87nctl display theme aurora
  e87nctl display refresh 2
  e87nctl display rotation on
  e87nctl display rotation off
  e87nctl display rotation-seconds 3
  e87nctl display pages overview,cpu,memory,thermal,fan,network,traffic,storage
  e87nctl display off
  e87nctl display on

Display settings: /etc/e87n/display.json
Module configuration: /etc/modules-load.d/e87n-display.conf
Both are dpkg conffiles. Use --force-confdef --force-confold with unattended
dpkg upgrades when existing local settings must take precedence.
Display write commands require root. The daemon reloads the validated config on
every refresh cycle, so theme, page and rotation changes normally need no
service restart. Brightness and logical on/off state are applied immediately.
`brightness 0` keeps sampling and drawing with a dark backlight; `display off`
also disables sampling and drawing while preserving the saved brightness.

Themes are dark, aurora and light colour skins over the same data semantics and
availability rules.
Pages are overview, cpu, memory, thermal, fan, network, traffic and storage.
All eight pages remain configurable. Missing telemetry hides its card, row and
automatic-rotation page. An unavailable fixed page temporarily falls back to
overview and returns to the configured page when telemetry recovers. The current
device has no usable storage-temperature telemetry, so storage is configurable
but skipped at runtime.
The traffic page shows cumulative RX/TX totals and measured receive/transmit
rates calculated from consecutive monotonic samples. The first sample after a
start, counter reset or long pause is unknown instead of an invented zero. The
fan page shows user-facing mode, cooling level and PWM percentage; internal
control strings and unsupported RPM values are not displayed.

Network cards are filtered before layout. `carrier=0` always hides a port,
regardless of stale addresses or counters. With unknown carrier, a port is shown
only when it has a valid IPv4 or global IPv6 address; link-local IPv6 alone is
not enough. A single visible port uses a full-width card.
Automatic page rotation is disabled by default; enable it with `e87nctl display
rotation on` and choose a 2-60 second interval with `rotation-seconds`.
Set `rotation off` before `screen PAGE` when a fixed page is required. The pages
command only saves the rotation list and order; it does not enable rotation.

The service e87n-display.service is enabled at installation, respecting
administrator disable/mask choices on upgrades. Image builds must supply
an executable /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d returning 101 to inhibit activation.
An ordinary image chroot has no running systemd. The package neither starts
hardware directly nor creates or replaces policy-rc.d.

Before removal, run `e87nctl display off` to switch off the backlight. Stopping
the service or removing the package alone can leave the last framebuffer image
and backlight visible. Removal stops the service and preserves conffiles; purge
removes the package's conffiles and helper state. Other board data and
administrator overrides are not recursively deleted. Service errors do not
block package configuration; inspect systemctl status e87n-display.service and
its journal after boot.

The complete Chinese update, configuration, rollback and troubleshooting guide
is maintained at:
https://github.com/baozaodetudou/EDGEPI-E87N/blob/main/docs/DISPLAY-USER-GUIDE.md
